/* ============================================================
   Not Organic — account portal
   ------------------------------------------------------------
   This surface used to be a dark green dashboard with an amber
   accent: a competent piece of design that belonged to a
   different company than the one on notorganic.info. Someone
   signing in went from a warm off-white paper site to a dark
   console and had to re-learn where they were. So the portal now
   takes the marketing site's palette, type, radii, and texture
   directly, and the join is meant to be invisible.

   Two things did NOT come across, on purpose:

   - The display scale. The site opens with a 5.9rem headline
     because it has one thing to say. A portal has forty, and
     numbers you have to compare. Headings here top out at
     2.6rem and the layout is built for density.
   - The hero photograph on every panel. Imagery earns its place
     at the sign-in step, where there is nothing else to look at
     and something to feel. Behind a table of charges it is just
     an obstacle to reading the table.

   PRODUCT.md, on this surface specifically: "Let nature-derived
   colour and real imagery carry warmth without making account
   controls decorative."
